{"tool":"web_run","args":{"open":[{"ref_id":"turn42search17"},{"ref_id":"turn42search35"},{"ref_id":"turn42search3"},{"ref_id":"turn42search16"},{"ref_id":"turn42search0"}],"response_length":"long"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Chat - Composer - MUI X (https://mui.com/x/react-chat/material/composer/)\n【turn43view0】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn42search17\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 339\nL0: 【0†Skip to content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†🚀 Material UI and MUI X v9 are out! Check out the announcement blogpost.】Search…\nL3: \nL4: MUI X\nL5: \nL6: Chat[Button: v9.0.0-alpha.20]\nL7: \nL8:   * 【2†What's new in MUI X】\nL9:   * 【3†Introduction】\nL10:   * 【4†Common concepts】\nL11:   * 【5†Data Grid】\nL12:   * 【6†Date and Time Pickers】\nL13:   * 【7†Charts】\nL14:   * 【8†Tree View】\nL15:   * 【9†Scheduler Preview】\nL16:   * 【10†Chat Preview】\nL17:   * 【11†Migration】\nL18: # Chat - Composer\nL19: \nL20: Compose and send chat messages with attachments, toolbar actions, and helper text.\nL21: \nL22:   * 【12†Feedback†github.com】\nL23:   * 【13†Bundle size†bundlephobia.com】\nL24:   * 【14†Figma】\nL25:   * 【15†Sketch】\nL26: \nL27: The composer is the input region at the bottom of the chat surface. `ChatComposer` provides Material UI styling—border, padding, and theme tokens are applied automatically.\nL28: ## 【16†Import】\nL29: \nL30:     `import {\nL31:       ChatComposer,\nL32:       ChatComposerLabel,\nL33:       ChatComposerTextArea,\nL34:       ChatComposerSendButton,\nL35:       ChatComposerAttachButton,\nL36:       ChatComposerToolbar,\nL37:       ChatComposerHelperText,\nL38:     } from '@mui/x-chat';\nL39:     `\nL40: \nL41: Copy Copied(or C)\nL42: \nL43: When using `ChatBox`, the composer is already included. Import these components directly only when building a custom layout.\nL44: ## 【17†Component anatomy】\nL45: Inside `ChatBox`, the composer renders the following structure:\nL46: \nL47:     `ChatComposer                  ← <form> element, border-top divider\nL48:       ChatComposerLabel           ← optional <label> for accessibility\nL49:       ChatComposerTextArea        ← auto-resizing textarea\nL50:       ChatComposerToolbar         ← button row\nL51:         ChatComposerAttachButton  ← file attach trigger\nL52:         ChatComposerSendButton    ← submit button (disabled when empty with no attachments/streaming)\nL53:       ChatComposerHelperText      ← disclaimer or character count\nL54:     `\nL55: Copy Copied(or C)\nL56: ## 【18†Text area】\nL57: \nL58: `ChatComposerTextArea` is an auto-resizing `<textarea>` that grows with content. It submits on Enter and inserts a newline on Shift+Enter.\nL59: \nL60: ### 【19†Customizing the placeholder】\nL61: \nL62: Customize the placeholder through `slotProps`:\nL63: \nL64: Material UI chat\nL65: \nL66: Styled with your active MUI theme\nL67: \nL68: MUI Assistant\nL69: \nL70: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL71: \nL72: You\nL73: \nL74: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL75: \nL76: [Input]\nL77: ### 【20†IME composition】\nL78: \nL79: The composer handles IME (Input Method Editor) composition for CJK languages. While the user is composing characters (for example, selecting Kanji), pressing Enter confirms the character selection instead of submitting the message. Submission is blocked until composition ends.\nL80: ## 【21†Send button】\nL81: \nL82: The send button is automatically disabled when:\nL83: \nL84:   * The text area is empty and there are no queued attachments.\nL85:   * A response is currently streaming.\nL86:   * The composer is explicitly disabled.\nL87: ## 【22†Attach button】\nL88: \nL89: The attach button opens the browser file picker. Selected files are queued as draft attachments and previewed in the composer area.\nL90: \nL91: Set `features={{ attachments: false }}` to hide the attach button:\nL92: \nL93: Material UI chat\nL94: \nL95: Styled with your active MUI theme\nL96: \nL97: MUI Assistant\nL98: \nL99: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL100: \nL101: You\nL102: \nL103: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL104: ## 【23†Helper text】\nL105: \nL106: A helper text line appears below the composer. Use it for legal disclaimers, character counts, or contextual hints.\nL107: \nL108:     `{\nL109:       /* Hide the helper text */\nL110:     }\nL111:     <ChatBox adapter={adapter} features={{ helperText: false }} />;\nL112:     `\nL113: \nL114: Copy Copied(or C)\nL115: ## 【24†Controlling the composer value】\nL116: \nL117: Control the composer value externally through `ChatProvider`, or through the equivalent `ChatBox` props that forward to it. The demo below mirrors the current composer value above the chat surface:\nL118: \nL119: Composer value: (empty)\nL120: \nL121: Material UI chat\nL122: \nL123: Styled with your active MUI theme\nL124: \nL125: MUI Assistant\nL126: \nL127: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL128: \nL129: You\nL130: \nL131: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL134: For deeper control, the `useChatComposer()` hook provides direct access to the composer state:\nL135: \nL136:     `import { useChatComposer } from '@mui/x-chat/headless';\nL137: \nL138:     function ComposerInfo() {\nL139:       const composer = useChatComposer();\nL140:       return (\nL141:         <div>\nL142:           <p>Current value: {composer.value}.</p>\nL143:           <p>Attachments: {composer.attachments.length}.</p>\nL144:           <p>Submitting: {composer.isSubmitting ? 'Yes' : 'No'}.</p>\nL153: Property  | Type  | Description\nL154: --- | --- | ---\nL155: `value`  | `string`  | Current text value\nL156: `setValue`  | `(value: string) => void`  | Update the text value\nL157: `attachments`  | `ChatDraftAttachment[]`  | Queued file attachments\nL158: `addAttachment`  | `(file: File) => void`  | Add a file to the draft\nL159: `removeAttachment`  | `(localId: string) => void`  | Remove a queued file\nL160: `clear`  | `() => void`  | Reset value and attachments\nL161: `submit`  | `() => Promise<void>`  | Submit the current draft\nL163: ### 【26†ChatDraftAttachment】\nL164: \nL165: The attachment type used by the composer:\nL166: \nL167: Property  | Type  | Description\nL168: --- | --- | ---\nL169: `localId`  | `string`  | Unique identifier for this draft attachment\nL170: `file`  | `File`  | The browser File object\nL171: `previewUrl`  | `string | undefined`  | Object URL for image previews (auto-created)\nL172: `status`  | `'queued' | 'uploading' | 'uploaded' | 'error'`  | Upload lifecycle status\nL173: `progress`  | `number | undefined`  | Upload progress (0–100)\nL174: ## 【27†Compact composer variants】\nL175: \nL176: The demo below shows five design ideas for the compact composer variant—click into the text area to see the focus state.\nL177: \nL178: ###### 1 — Top separator\nL179: \nL180: Only a top border divider. Focus colors it primary.\nL181: \nL182: MUI Assistant\nL183: \nL184: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL185: \nL186: You\nL187: \nL188: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL189: \nL190: [Input]\nL191: ###### 2 — Floating pill\nL192: \nL193: Margin + pill-shaped radius. Focus adds primary ring.\nL194: \nL195: MUI Assistant\nL196: \nL197: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL198: \nL199: You\nL200: \nL201: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL202: \nL203: [Input]\nL204: ###### 3 — Elevated card\nL205: \nL206: No border, elevation shadow. Focus deepens shadow.\nL207: \nL208: MUI Assistant\nL209: \nL210: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL211: \nL212: You\nL213: \nL214: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL215: \nL216: [Input]\nL217: ###### 4 — Borderless minimal\nL218: \nL219: Top separator, transparent bg. Focus tints background.\nL220: \nL221: MUI Assistant\nL222: \nL223: Hello! I am styled using your active Material UI theme. Try sending a message.\nL224: \nL225: You\nL226: \nL227: Great — the bubble colors come from palette.primary and the typography from the theme.\nL228: \nL229: [Input]\nL230: ###### 5 — Inset outlined\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMessage Input - shadcn-chatbot-kit (https://shadcn-chatbot-kit.vercel.app/docs/components/message-input)\n【turn43view1】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn42search35\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 222\nL0: Toggle Menu\nL1: \nL2: Search...\nL3: \nL4: 【0†GitHub†github.com】【1†Twitter†twitter.com】Toggle theme\nL5: \nL6: #### Getting Started\nL7: \nL8: 【2†Introduction】【3†Installation】\nL9: \nL10: #### Components\nL11: \nL12: 【4†Chat】【5†Message Input】【6†Message List】【7†Chat Message】【8†Markdown Renderer】【9†Prompt Suggestions】【10†Typing Indicator】【11†Copy Button】【12†File Preview】【13†Audio Visualizer】\nL13: \nL14: Docs\nL15: \nL16: Message Input\nL17: # Message Input\nL18: \nL19: A textarea component with file attachment support, auto-resizing, and drag-and-drop capabilities.\nL20: \nL21: [Button: Preview][Button: Code]\nL22: \nL23: Copy\nL24: \nL25: The MessageInput component provides a rich textarea experience with support for file attachments, auto-resizing, and drag-and-drop file uploads.\nL26: ## Features\nL27: \nL28:   * Auto-resizing textarea\nL29:   * File attachments support\nL30:   * Drag and drop file uploads\nL31:   * Submit on Enter (configurable)\nL32:   * Stop generation button\nL33:   * Double-enter interrupt behavior\nL34:   * Voice input with transcription\nL35:   * Fully customizable styling\nL36: \nL37: ## Installation\nL38: \nL39: [Button: CLI][Button: Manual]\nL40: \nL41:     `npx shadcn@latest add https://shadcn-chatbot-kit.vercel.app/r/message-input.json`\nL42: \nL43: ## Usage\nL44: ### Basic Usage\nL45: \nL46:     `import { MessageInput } from \"@/components/ui/message-input\"\nL47: \nL48:     export function BasicMessageInput() {\nL49:       return (\nL50:         <MessageInput\nL51:           value={input}\nL52:           onChange={handleInputChange}\nL53:           isGenerating={false}\nL54:         />\nL55:       )\nL56:     }`\nL57: ### With Interrupt Behavior\nL58: \nL59:     `export function MessageInputWithInterrupt() {\nL60:       return (\nL61:         <MessageInput\nL62:           value={input}\nL63:           onChange={handleInputChange}\nL64:           isGenerating={isGenerating}\nL65:           stop={handleStop}\nL66:           enableInterrupt={true}\nL67:         />\nL68:       )\nL69:     }`\nL70: When `enableInterrupt` is enabled and `isGenerating` is true, pressing Enter once will show a prompt asking the user to press Enter again to interrupt the generation. The prompt will disappear either when the user presses Enter again (triggering the stop function) or when the generation completes.\nL71: ### With File Attachments\nL72: \nL73:     `import { MessageInput } from \"@/components/ui/message-input\"\nL74: \nL75:     export function MessageInputWithAttachments() {\nL76:       const [files, setFiles] = useState<File[] | null>(null)\nL77: \nL78:       return (\nL79:         <MessageInput\nL80:           value={input}\nL81:           onChange={handleInputChange}\nL82:           isGenerating={false}\nL83:           allowAttachments\nL84:           files={files}\nL85:           setFiles={setFiles}\nL86:         />\nL87:       )\nL88:     }`\nL89: ### With Stop Button\nL90: \nL91:     `import { MessageInput } from \"@/components/ui/message-input\"\nL92: \nL93:     export function MessageInputWithStop() {\nL94:       return (\nL95:         <MessageInput\nL96:           value={input}\nL97:           onChange={handleInputChange}\nL98:           isGenerating={true}\nL99:           stop={() => {\nL100:             // Handle stop generation\nL101:           }}\nL102:         />\nL103:       )\nL104:     }`\nL105: \nL106: ## Props\nL107: \nL108: The MessageInput component accepts two sets of props depending on whether file attachments are enabled.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nchatbot/components/ai-elements/prompt-input.tsx at main · vercel/chatbot · GitHub (https://github.com/vercel/chatbot/blob/main/components/ai-elements/prompt-input.tsx)\n【turn43view2】 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn42search3\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 3902\nL3459: const dataUrl = await convertBlobUrlToDataUrl(item.url);\nL3460: \nL3461: // If conversion failed, keep the original blob URL\nL3462: \nL3463: return {\nL3464: \nL3465: ...item,\nL3466: \nL3467: url: dataUrl ?? item.url,\nL3468: \nL3469: };\nL3470: \nL3471: }\nL3472: \nL3473: return item;\nL3474: \nL3475: })\nL3476: \nL3477: );\nL3478: \nL3479: const result = onSubmit({ files: convertedFiles, text }, event);\nL3480: \nL3481: // Handle both sync and async onSubmit\nL3482: \nL3483: if (result instanceof Promise) {\nL3484: \nL3485: try {\nL3486: \nL3487: await result;\nL3488: \nL3489: clear();\nL3490: \nL3491: if (usingProvider) {\nL3492: \nL3493: controller.textInput.clear();\nL3494: \nL3495: }\nL3496: \nL3497: } catch {\nL3498: \nL3499: // Don't clear on error - user may want to retry\nL3500: \nL3501: }\nL3502: \nL3503: } else {\nL3504: // Sync function completed without throwing, clear inputs\nL3505: \nL3506: clear();\nL3507: \nL3508: if (usingProvider) {\nL3509: \nL3510: controller.textInput.clear();\nL3511: \nL3512: }\nL3513: \nL3514: }\nL3515: \nL3516: } catch {\nL3517: \nL3518: // Don't clear on error - user may want to retry\nL3519: \nL3520: }\nL3521: \nL3522: },\nL3523: \nL3524: [usingProvider, controller, files, onSubmit, clear]\nL3525: \nL3526: );\nL3527: \nL3528: // Render with or without local provider\nL3529: \nL3530: const inner = (\nL3531: \nL3532: <>\nL3533: \nL3534: <input\nL3535: \nL3536: accept={accept}\nL3537: \nL3538: aria-label=\"Upload files\"\nL3539: \nL3540: className=\"hidden\"\nL3541: \nL3542: multiple={multiple}\nL3543: \nL3544: onChange={handleChange}\nL3545: \nL3546: ref={inputRef}\nL3547: \nL3548: title=\"Upload files\"\nL3549: \nL3550: type=\"file\"\nL3551: \nL3552: />\nL3553: \nL3554: <form\nL3555: className={cn(\"w-full\", className)}\nL3556: \nL3557: onSubmit={handleSubmit}\nL3558: \nL3559: ref={formRef}\nL3560: \nL3561: {...props}\nL3562: \nL3563: >\nL3564: \nL3565: <InputGroup className=\"overflow-hidden\">{children}</InputGroup>\nL3566: \nL3567: </form>\nL3568: \nL3569: </>\nL3570: \nL3571: );\nL3572: \nL3573: const withReferencedSources = (\nL3574: \nL3575: <LocalReferencedSourcesContext.Provider value={refsCtx}>\nL3576: \nL3577: {inner}\nL3578: \nL3579: </LocalReferencedSourcesContext.Provider>\nL3580: \nL3581: );\nL3582: \nL3583: // Always provide LocalAttachmentsContext so children get validated add function\nL3584: \nL3585: return (\nL3586: \nL3587: <LocalAttachmentsContext.Provider value={attachmentsCtx}>\nL3588: \nL3589: {withReferencedSources}\nL3590: </LocalAttachmentsContext.Provider>\nL3591: \nL3592: );\nL3593: \nL3594: };\nL3595: \nL3596: export type PromptInputBodyProps = HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>;\nL3597: \nL3598: export const PromptInputBody = ({\nL3599: \nL3600: className,\nL3601: \nL3602: ...props\nL3603: \nL3604: }: PromptInputBodyProps) => (\nL3605: \nL3606: <div className={cn(\"contents\", className)} {...props} />\nL3607: \nL3608: );\nL3609: \nL3610: export type PromptInputTextareaProps = ComponentProps<\nL3611: \nL3612: typeof InputGroupTextarea\nL3613: \nL3614: >;\nL3615: \nL3616: export const PromptInputTextarea = (