ToBottom` resumes it. A new run or a thread switch also ends the pause. Set `autoScroll={false}` to disable this entirely.\nL114: \nL115:     `<ThreadPrimitive.Viewport autoScroll={true}>\nL116:       {/* messages */}\nL117:     </ThreadPrimitive.Viewport>`\nL118: ### 【27†Turn Anchor】\nL119: \nL120: By default, new messages appear at the bottom and scroll down. With `turnAnchor=\"top\"`, the user's message anchors to the top of the viewport. The question stays at the top and the response streams in below it.\nL121: \nL122:     `<ThreadPrimitive.Viewport turnAnchor=\"top\">\nL123:       {/* messages */}\nL124:     </ThreadPrimitive.Viewport>`\nL125: When `turnAnchor=\"top\"` is set, `MessagePrimitive.Root` registers the latest assistant message as the top-anchor target and the preceding user message as the anchor, so no additional component is required. The viewport itself manages a stable reserve element that provides the missing scroll range while the assistant response grows. This is the behavior used by the 【28†Thread】 component by default.\n"}],"isError":false}}
